    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0275" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J.C.S. Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Representatives of the British
                        Chiefs of Staff</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/> C.C.S. 654/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-02">2 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Basic Policies for the Next
                        United States-British Staff Conference</hi></p>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell>References:</cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>. C.C.S. 654<anchor n="1"
                                xml:id="d141-f1"/></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>. C.C.S. 426/1<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d141-f2"/></cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>1. The British Chiefs of Staff recommend acceptance of the following amendments
                    to the proposals put forward by the United States Chiefs of Staff in C.C.S.
                    654.</p>
                <pb facs="0276" n="220" xml:id="pg220"/>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Paragraph 6 f</hi>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p><hi rendition="#italic">f</hi>. <del rendition="#strikethrough"
                                >Continue</del>
                            <del rendition="#strikethrough">to</del>
                            <del rendition="#strikethrough">aid</del>
                            <del rendition="#strikethrough">the</del>
                            <del rendition="#strikethrough">war</del>
                            <del rendition="#strikethrough">effort</del>
                            <del rendition="#strikethrough">of</del>
                            <del rendition="#strikethrough">Russia.</del><anchor n="3"
                                xml:id="d141-f3"/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Undertake such measures as may be necessary and
                                practicable to aid the war effort of Russia including the
                                coordinated action of our forces</hi>.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d141-f4"
                            /></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>This wording was used in C.C.S. 426/1, paragraph 6 <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >g</hi>, and the British Chiefs of Staff feel that the coordination of action of
                    our forces with the Russians will be of increasing importance as they
                    converge.</p>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Paragraph 6 h</hi>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p><hi rendition="#italic">h</hi>. Continue assistance to the French and
                            Italian forces, <hi rendition="#italic">and be prepared to assist other
                                co-belligerents</hi>, to enable them to fulfill an active role in
                            the war against the Axis Powers.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>This amendment is designed to cover, for example, supplies to Turkey and Axis
                    satellites turning over to our side.</p>
                <p>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">Paragraph 6 i</hi>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p><hi rendition="#italic">i</hi>. Reorient forces from the European Theater
                            to the Pacific and Far East as a matter of highest priority <hi
                                rendition="#italic">having regard to other in escapable
                                commitments</hi> as soon as the German situation allows.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>2. In all other respects the proposals put forward are acceptable to the British
                    Chiefs of Staff.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
